doc Bitwise-xor assignment: x ^= y, short for x = x ^ y.
  ```
  let n = 12
  n ^= 10
  print n           // 6
  ```

  The left side can be any place of type `int`: a variable, a field, a
  slice element or `*p`, evaluated once.

needs std/let std/addr std/deref std/assign std/bxor
syntax statement
  {x: place int} ^= {y: expr int}
expand
  let {$p} = &{x}
  *{$p} = *{$p} ^ {y}
